(i)   $2Fe_{2} O_{3}$(s) $\to$ 4Fe(s) + $3O_{2}$(g);

$\Delta$_{r}$G^{o}$ = + 1487.0 kJ $mol^{-1}$

(ii)   2CO(g) + $O_{2}$(g) $\to 2CO_{2}$(g);

$\Delta$_{r}$G^{o} = -$ 514.4 kJ $mol^{-1}$

Multiply reaction (ii) with  3 and we get,

(iii)   6CO(g) + $3O_{2}$ (g)    $\buildrel \, \over \longrightarrow 6CO_{2}$(g) ;

$\Delta$_{r}$G^{o}$ = 3 $\times -$ 514.4 =  -  1543.2 kJ mol^{ - 1}

Now add reaction (i)   with  (iii),  we get

$2Fe_{2} O_{3}$(s) + 6CO(g)    $\buildrel \, \over \longrightarrow$    4Fe(s) + $6CO_{2}$(g)

$\therefore\,\,\,$ Free energy change of the reaction,

$\Delta$_{r}$G^{o}$  =  1487.0  -  1543.2  =  $-$ 56.2 kJ/mol

